# The allowlist of tests/retired_words.rs (RFC 012 D-4): a user-facing message may not use a word the plain-word
# rewrite retired, except where the word is not ours to change. Reviewed like code: a line added here is a decision.
#
# key :: term :: reason
#   key     the message key (for example `verify.intro`)
#   term    the retired word or label the message is allowed to contain
#   reason  why it is legitimate (data owned by prikk, the name of a command in operator text, ...)
#
# An entry that no message needs any more fails the test, so this file cannot collect dead lines. It is empty
# today: no message of the English catalog uses a retired word.
